RigMatch is source-available, not open source.

The source code is published so that anyone can read it, audit it, and verify
what the application does — in particular, that it runs models locally and does
not send your data anywhere. You are welcome to read it for that purpose.

No rights to use the source code are granted beyond reading it. Copying,
distributing, modifying, or creating derivative works from this software or its
source code, in whole or in part, is prohibited without the express written
permission of the copyright owner.

Using the released application itself is, of course, fine — that is what it is
for.
